{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ufpyDeDNqW1vSdWgeSK2v","type":"tool_result","content":"# Tickets\n\nWork through the tickets in order. A ticket can start once every ticket in its\n**Blocked by** line is done. The specification is [`../README.md`](../README.md); each\nticket names the sections it implements and the acceptance criteria it must satisfy.\n\n| # | Ticket | Blocked by | Criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | [Movie list and day picker](01-movie-list.md) | — | 11 |\n| 02 | [Auditorium map](02-auditorium-map.md) | 01 | 13 |\n| 03 | [Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel](03-seat-selection.md) | 02 | 14 |\n| 04 | [Booking and summary](04-booking-summary.md) | 03 | 16 |\n| 05 | [Checkout and payment](05-checkout.md) | 04 | 13 |\n| 06 | [Confirmation and booking lifecycle](06-confirmation.md) | 05 | 2 |\n| 07 | [Final pass](07-final-pass.md) | 01–06 | all |\n\nA ticket is done when every box in it is ticked and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n# 01: Movie list and day picker\n\n**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n\n**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by de","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f36d358a-b9a0-405d-bd0d-b9be109acf26","uuid":"7191f686-ede4-4c0f-bfbb-88af4be9fee7","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:54:30.762Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Tickets\n\nWork through the tickets in order. A ticket can start once every ticket in its\n**Blocked by** line is done. The specification is [`../README.md`](../README.md); each\nticket names the sections it implements and the acceptance criteria it must satisfy.\n\n| # | Ticket | Blocked by | Criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | [Movie list and day picker](01-movie-list.md) | — | 11 |\n| 02 | [Auditorium map](02-auditorium-map.md) | 01 | 13 |\n| 03 | [Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel](03-seat-selection.md) | 02 | 14 |\n| 04 | [Booking and summary](04-booking-summary.md) | 03 | 16 |\n| 05 | [Checkout and payment](05-checkout.md) | 04 | 13 |\n| 06 | [Confirmation and booking lifecycle](06-confirmation.md) | 05 | 2 |\n| 07 | [Final pass](07-final-pass.md) | 01–06 | all |\n\nA ticket is done when every box in it is ticked and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n# 01: Movie list and day picker\n\n**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n\n**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by de","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
