{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTcbnmGDSR41UPFwXmNG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AB76RX3ReBwViiAn81vr9J","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat spec/README.md | head -c 40000 | tail -c +2000","description":"Read full spec README in pieces"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1692,"cache_read_input_tokens":24760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1692,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ptct5JmRojLzBbfcaTvZLd","session_id":"f36d358a-b9a0-405d-bd0d-b9be109acf26","uuid":"145ac54d-ca0a-48fd-a0fc-b435e64f4787","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:57:04.317Z","request_id":"req_011ChTcbnfJnufpVNA9nRMf4","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 02"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AB76RX3ReBwViiAn81vr9J","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (29.7KB). Full output saved to: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/f36d358a-b9a0-405d-bd0d-b9be109acf26/tool-results/b18qlbu55.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\npplication.\n\n- **Base URL:** `http://localhost:3000`\n- CORS is enabled; the application calls the base URL directly.\n- Every response is JSON. Requests with a body send `Content-Type: application/json`.\n- `json-server` writes every successful `POST` into `db.json`. That is expected.\n\n### 2.1 Data model\n\n```ts\ninterface Movie {\n  id: number;\n  title: string;            // \"The Silent Harbor\"\n  genre: string;            // \"Drama\"\n  runtimeMinutes: number;   // 128\n  format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles';\n}\n\ninterface Screening {\n  id: number;\n  movieId: number;          // references Movie.id\n  date: string;             // \"2026-09-15\" (YYYY-MM-DD)\n  time: string;             // \"16:00\" (HH:mm, 24-hour)\n  occupiedSeats: string[];  // seat identifiers already sold, e.g. [\"R3C7\", \"R15C5\", \"R15C6\"]\n}\n\ninterface Reservation {\n  id: number;               // assigned by the backend\n  screeningId: number;\n  seats: string[];          // seat identifiers, a couch contributes both of its identifiers\n  customer: {\n    firstName: string;\n    lastName: string;\n    email: string;\n    phone: string;          // \"\" when not provided\n  };\n  totalPrice: number;       // in PLN, e.g. 121\n}\n```\n\n**Seat identifier** — `R<row>C<column>`, for example `R7C12` is row 7, column 12. A couch\noccupies two identifiers: the couch over columns 5–6 of row 15 is `R15C5` + `R15C6`.\n\n### 2.2 Endpoints\n\n| Method | Path | Returns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET` | `/movies` | `Movie[]` — 5 movies |\n| `GET` | `/movies/:id` | `Movie`, or `404` |\n| `GET` | `/screenings` | `Screening[]` — all screenings, in no guaranteed order |\n| `GET` | `/screenings?date=:date` | `Screening[]` of one day, e.g. `?date=2026-09-15` |\n| `GET` | `/screenings?movieId=:movieId` | `Screening[]` of one movie |\n| `GET` | `/screenings/:id` | `Screening`, or `404` |\n| `POST` | `/reservations` | `201` with the created `Reservation` |\n\n`GET /screenings/1` returns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"movieId\": 1,\n  \"date\": \"2026-09-15\",\n  \"time\": \"16:00\",\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ptct5JmRojLzBbfcaTvZLd","session_id":"f36d358a-b9a0-405d-bd0d-b9be109acf26","uuid":"11180137-366f-44f3-ae04-a2f7f2d5dd45","timestamp":"2026-11-27T13:57:04.348Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 02"}
