{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011L3P1XrFMaLrms4nxGrhKG","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (34.9KB). Full output saved to: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/f36d358a-b9a0-405d-bd0d-b9be109acf26/tool-results/b1s3dq5rd.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Cinescope — cinema seat booking\n\nA web application for booking cinema seats. A customer picks a day and a movie screening,\nchooses seats on a map of the auditorium, reviews the tickets, fills in their details and\npays.\n\nThis file is the complete specification. The work is split into tickets in\n[`tickets/`](tickets/README.md); each ticket points back to the sections below and lists\nthe acceptance criteria it has to satisfy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project setup\n\nThe framework, the libraries and the state of the scaffold are described in\n[`stack.md`](stack.md). The application is the Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`.\n\nAll commands run from the workspace root:\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `pnpm install` | installs dependencies (already done) |\n| `pnpm nx serve cinescope` | starts the application at `http://localhost:4200` |\n| `pnpm api` | starts the backend at `http://localhost:3000` |\n| `pnpm nx build cinescope` | production build — must succeed |\n| `pnpm nx test cinescope` | unit tests (Vitest) |\n| `pnpm nx lint cinescope` | ESLint |\n\nRules for the environment:\n\n- The package manager is pnpm. Do not use `npm` or `yarn`.\n- The application is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Do not change the port.\n- Do not add dependencies. Everything the application needs is already installed.\n- Do not edit `db.json` by hand. It is the backend's data.\n- The application is desktop-only (viewport 1280 × 720 or larger). All user-facing text is\n  in English.\n\n### 1.1 UI library\n\nUse components of the UI library named in [`stack.md`](stack.md) for every button (including the day buttons and the\nscreening buttons), text field, checkbox, toast and for the datepicker. The seat map, the\nlegend and the selected-seats panel are drawn by the application itself.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Backend\n\nThe backend is [`json-server`](https://github.com/typicode/json-server/tree/v0) 0.17.4\nserving `db.json` from the workspace root. Start it with `pnpm api` and keep it running\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KsbhaE4tCvdQHk5TDJf3BK","session_id":"f36d358a-b9a0-405d-bd0d-b9be109acf26","uuid":"f4d6341c-0418-4e8a-ad8c-2eb5f980c9d1","timestamp":"2026-11-27T14:01:18.574Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 04"}
